# Exceptions of the vulnerability gate (design D4, D9).
#
# The Scan stage always passes this file to Trivy with --ignorefile, so an
# exception is versioned, appears in the diff and is reviewed in the pull
# request that adds it. It is the only way to silence a finding: no pipeline
# parameter skips the scan and --ignore-unfixed is deliberately absent (D9).
#
# One finding per line, with its justification and an expiry date right above
# it, so a stale exception is visible where it is declared:
#
#   # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN: expires YYYY-MM-DD - reason
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#
# The file ships without entries: the gate breaks the build on every HIGH or
# CRITICAL finding, and an exception only enters when a real false positive
# justifies it.
